        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 rounded-2xl p-8 text-gray-200">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">
            Wet pressure-treated lumber needs four weeks to three months; KDAT and kiln-dried cedar need a clean and a few days. Nothing needs a year. The wood is ready when water soaks in rather than beading and a meter reads under 15 percent, and not before.
          </p>
          <p class="m-0">
            Clean and brighten even a brand-new deck, let it dry, test it, then apply one thin coat of a penetrating oil and brush it in. Do that on time and the deck never needs stripping. Do it too early and you will be stripping it next spring.
          </p>
        </div>

